            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous coronary intervention of a totally occluded anomalous right coronary artery arising from the left sinus of valsalva with the use of multiple overlapping drug-eluting stents (&quot;full-metal jacket&quot; technique).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E261-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary arterial anomalies occur in approximately 1% of the population, without other congenital cardiac malformations. We report our experience involving 1 patient who had a totally occluded anomalous right coronary artery arising from the left sinus of Valsalva which was successfully treated with the implantation of multiple overlapping drug-eluting stents (&quot;full-metal jacket&quot; technique).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
